{"id": "release-code-toposort", "kind": "code", "family": "toposort", "passed": false, "reason": "execution or assertion failure", "text": "```python\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n\ndef toposort(graph: dict) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a valid topological ordering of nodes in the graph.\n    \n    graph: a dict mapping a node to its dependencies (list of nodes that must come before it).\n    Returns: a list of nodes such that for every dependency d in graph[n], d appears before n.\n    Raises: ValueError if a cycle is detected.\n    \"\"\"\n    visited = set()\n    rec_stack = set()\n    result = []\n\n    def dfs(node):\n        if node in rec_stack:\n            raise ValueError(\"Cycle detected in the graph\")\n        if node in visited:\n            return\n\n        visited.add(node)\n        rec_stack.add(node)\n\n        for dep in graph.get(node, []):\n            if dep not in visited:\n                dfs(dep)\n\n        rec_stack.remove(node)\n        result.append(node)\n\n    # Ensure all nodes in the graph are processed\n    all_nodes = set(graph.keys())\n    for deps in graph.values():\n        all_nodes.update(deps)\n\n    for node in all_nodes:\n        if node not in visited:\n            dfs(node)\n\n    return result\n```", "tool_calls": [], "finish_reason": "stop", "input_tokens": 75, "output_tokens": 263, "seconds": 4.052, "tokens_per_second": 70.65, "peak_memory_gb": 3.861}
{"id": "release-code-deepmerge", "kind": "code", "family": "deepmerge", "passed": true, "reason": "passed", "text": "```python\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Union\n\ndef deep_merge(a: Dict[Any, Any], b: Dict[Any, Any]) -> Dict[Any, Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Recursively merge two dictionaries.\n    - Values from b replace non-dict conflicts.\n    - Nested dicts are merged recursively.\n    - Neither input is mutated.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = deepcopy(a)\n    \n    for key, value in b.items():\n        if key in result:\n            existing = result[key]\n            if isinstance(existing, dict) and isinstance(value, dict):\n                result[key] = deep_merge(existing, value)\n            else:\n                result[key] = value\n        else:\n            result[key] = value\n            \n    return result\n```", "tool_calls": [], "finish_reason": "stop", "input_tokens": 72, "output_tokens": 172, "seconds": 2.781, "tokens_per_second": 69.95, "peak_memory_gb": 3.861}
{"id": "release-code-window", "kind": "code", "family": "window", "passed": true, "reason": "passed", "text": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef moving_average(values: List[float], width: int) -> List[float]:\n    if width <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"width must be positive\")\n    \n    if width > len(values):\n        return []\n    \n    result = []\n    current_sum = sum(values[:width])\n    result.append(current_sum / width)\n    \n    for i in range(width, len(values)):\n        current_sum = current_sum + values[i] - values[i - width]\n        result.append(current_sum / width)\n    \n    return result\n```", "tool_calls": [], "finish_reason": "stop", "input_tokens": 72, "output_tokens": 126, "seconds": 2.105, "tokens_per_second": 70.33, "peak_memory_gb": 3.861}
